# Corpora acquired after the 2026-08-04 history purge. Same rule as above:
# source transcripts are licensed by their publishers and never redistributed
# from this public repo. Scripts and derived results are tracked; raw text is not.
analysis/s10/us/
analysis/s10/provinces/
analysis/s10/permeation/
# ...but the download and extraction SCRIPTS in those directories are our own
# work and contain no source text. They are the only path from a recorded
# seg_id back to the text it names, so without them the verdict files are
# unreproducible for 17 of the 21 chambers. Un-ignore them explicitly.
!analysis/s10/us/
!analysis/s10/us/*.py
!analysis/s10/provinces/
!analysis/s10/provinces/*.py

# RE-IGNORE the data inside those directories. Un-ignoring a DIRECTORY makes
# git descend into it again, so the two lines above silently undid the whole
# rule: 38 raw-transcript directories were left merely UNTRACKED rather than
# ignored, and a single `git add -A` would have staged licensed source text
# into a public repo. Found 2026-08-13 during the chamber backfill. The
# un-ignores must stay narrow (scripts only) and every data directory under
# them must be named again here.
analysis/s10/us/*/
analysis/s10/provinces/*_raw*/
# ...and the same names WITHOUT a trailing slash: two of the raw dirs
# (aus_nsw2025_raw, aus_qld_2025_raw) are symlinks, and a dir-only pattern
# does not match a symlink.
analysis/s10/provinces/*_raw
analysis/s10/provinces/work/
analysis/s10/provinces/*.out
analysis/s10/provinces/*.log
analysis/s10/*/xml_*/
analysis/s10/*/zips/

# Pangram upload pools: RTF/CSV batches carrying Hansard verbatim.
analysis/s10/pangram_ch/
analysis/s10/pangram_ch2/
analysis/s10/pangram_genre/
analysis/s10/pangram_x/
analysis/s10/pangram_rtf/
analysis/s10/pangram_web_scans/
analysis/s10/pangram_shortband/
analysis/s10/pangram_tier_check/
analysis/s10/pangram_ch_rescore/
analysis/s10/pangram_mb_redraw/
analysis/s10/olmo_ladder/

# Full third-party transcripts: quote from them in notes, never redistribute whole
reading/notes/*-transcript.txt

# Extracted-speech pools: derived from the corpora, but they carry the source
# text verbatim, so they inherit its licence and stay out of the public repo.
analysis/s10/align_ratio/
analysis/s10/word_context/
# quality_expansion: ignore only the blinded TEXT pools, which carry Hansard
# verbatim. The scripts, unblinding keys (metadata only) and graded results
# (scores only) carry no source text and are tracked, so the quality arm is
# reproducible from the repo given the corpora.
analysis/s10/quality_expansion/pool*.json
# Rewritten variants: not verbatim Hansard, but close paraphrases preserving
# every argument and claim, so they inherit the same licence question. Held
# locally; tracked result files keep ids, scores and hypotheses.
analysis/s10/bypass_text/
analysis/s10/quality_expansion/judge_blind_pool*.json
analysis/s10/band_screen_pool.json

# Scratch download areas and large run inputs — acquired sources, not our work.
analysis/s9/profiling/runs/
analysis/_scratch_ins/
fetched/

# Acquired papers live beside the analysis that cites them, but are never
# committed — the guard blocks them too. Scripts and results are versioned.
analysis/*/profiling/*.pdf
analysis/**/*.pdf
!analysis/**/METHODOLOGY*.pdf
!analysis/**/REVIEW*.pdf

# Short-band upload CSVs: verbatim Hansard, same licence policy as the other
# corpus text. The manifest (ids + metadata) and the verdicts (labels only)
# are tracked, so the arm is reproducible from build_shortband.py + corpora.
analysis/s10/pangram_shortband/
analysis/s10/pangram_tier_check/
analysis/s10/pangram_ch_rescore/
analysis/s10/pangram_mb_redraw/

# Superseded Manitoba raw extraction (176MB) -- kept on disk so the pre-fix
# verdicts stay reproducible, referenced by S10-WRITEUP-DRAFT footnote r42mb,
# but not tracked; rebuildable from the archived downloads.
analysis/s10/provinces/superseded/
# Rebuildable per-member vector cache (14MB): python build_member_vectors.py
analysis/s10/member_word_vectors.json

